WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:04.650
The 2019 iPad Air has just been released,
but there’s a problem, it’s basically

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:10.760
the 2017 10.5” iPad Pro, but with a newer
processor and a few missing features, for

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:11.920
almost as much cash.

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:18.019
And we’ve seen the 2017 Pro for as low as
$400 on Amazon, even cheaper than the Air,

00:00:18.019 --> 00:00:21.579
so make sure to check the links in the description
to see if it’s still on sale.

00:00:21.579 --> 00:00:22.609
So what’s the difference?

00:00:22.609 --> 00:00:23.609
And how do you choose?

00:00:23.609 --> 00:00:25.210
Well, let’s compare them!

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:29.659
On the backside, they look almost identical,
except that the old Pro has a camera bump

00:00:29.659 --> 00:00:30.810
and flash.

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:35.180
On the top edge, you’ll find two extra speakers
on the Pro, which is the biggest reason to

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:36.470
get the Pro instead.

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:41.190
We also get the same smart connector on the
side of each iPad for the smart keyboard.

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:43.760
On the front, they look literally identical.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:49.360
They get the same resolution, same laminated
display, same true tone and p3 wide-color

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:53.360
gamut, but the Air is actually missing ProMotion
technology.

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:58.040
What this means is that it allows the display
to refresh at up to 120Hz and dynamically

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:02.500
go down to match the frame rate of the content
you’re viewing to save battery life.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:08.270
As you can see in this slow-mo clip of the
2018 iPad Pro and 2019 iPad Air, the difference

00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:11.630
in the smoothness of ProMotion compared to
the Air is huge!

00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:14.040
And trust me, you’ll feel this difference
every day!

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:19.049
Not only that, but ProMotion lowers the latency
of the Apple Pencil as well, and you can easily

00:01:19.049 --> 00:01:22.600
see the difference compared to the iPad Air
which doesn’t have it.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:28.679
The 2017 iPad Pro’s display also gets brighter,
at 600 nits compared to 500 on the new Air,

00:01:28.679 --> 00:01:30.659
so that means it supports HDR video.

00:01:30.659 --> 00:02:06.310
Now let’s listen to a quick sound comparison
between these iPads.

00:02:06.310 --> 00:02:10.050
As you guys heard, most of the sound is coming
from the right side on the Air, so you get

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:14.860
a much better listening experience on the
Pro, not to mention actual stereo separation

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:16.190
in landscape mode.

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:19.830
This is gonna be huge if you’re into gaming,
allowing you to easily hear footsteps around

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:21.200
you in shooting games.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:24.920
Before we compare performance and gaming,
let’s compare the cameras.

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:31.720
The 2017 iPad Pro actually has a better rear
camera than the Air, at 12MP instead of 8.

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:34.580
This means you can take better photos and
shoot 4K video.

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:38.200
Here’s a quick photo comparison so you can
see the difference.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:44.110
Getting into performance, the 2019 iPad Air
gets the new A12 processor from the iPhone

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:49.930
XS, complete with the neural engine, and the
2017 iPad Pro gets an older A10X chip, but

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:54.460
the Pro actually gets 4GB of RAM compared
to 3 on the new Air.

00:02:54.460 --> 00:03:01.290
Comparing Geekbench 4 scores, the Air is 22%
faster in single-core and 21% faster in multi-core,

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:04.180
which is definitely a difference, but not
that much.

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:09.510
Comparing the Metal graphics performance test,
the old iPad Pro is actually 35% faster than

00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:14.170
the new Air, which affects gaming performance
more than processor performance does.

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:19.600
Now testing the Antutu benchmark, the new
Air is now 35% faster than the old Pro, a

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:20.670
pretty good difference.

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:26.180
We decided to test a more realistic test by
exporting a 1 minute 4K HEVC video, and the

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:31.040
iPad Air finished 18 seconds sooner than the
old Pro, which is surprisingly not that big

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:32.070
of a difference.

00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:34.090
Now let’s compare gaming performance.

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:39.010
Playing Fortnite, both iPads can play at 60
frames per second, but the old Pro is limited

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:44.120
to Medium graphics in this setting, while
the new Air can run 60fps on High settings.

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:48.750
In game, both of them are incredibly smooth
and responsive, with no noticeable dropped

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:50.510
frames at 60 fps.

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:53.120
The biggest difference I noticed was actually
the speakers.

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:57.280
It was hard to hear footsteps on the Air with
speakers only on one side.

00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:00.819
So it seems like the Air is going to have
better gaming performance with higher settings

00:04:00.819 --> 00:04:04.430
in certain game, but both iPads run games
perfectly.

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:09.870
The Air also gets newer cellular and wireless
tech like Bluetooth 5.0, simultaneous dual-band

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:12.530
WiFi and Gigabit-class LTE.

00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:18.600
So here’s the question, since you can find
the 2017 iPad Pro for $500-$570 brand new

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:24.840
or for only $400 refurbished on Amazon, is
the extra performance of the 2019 iPad Air

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:31.810
worth missing out on the iPad Pro’s awesome
ProMotion technology and four-speaker audio?

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:36.001
Going back to a non-Pro iPad feels really
weird because it’s missing ProMotion, it

00:04:36.001 --> 00:04:38.950
feels like the processor is slow but it really
isn’t.

00:04:38.950 --> 00:04:43.470
Same for the speakers, once you experience
four speakers on the Pro, it’s really hard

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:44.470
to go back.

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:49.630
In my opinion, those features make the 2017
10.5” iPad Pro a much better value than

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:55.310
the Air, as long as you can find it on sale
below $600, which it currently is on Amazon,

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:57.820
so make sure to check the links in the description
below.

00:04:57.820 --> 00:05:02.380
The only caveat is that the Pro will lose
software support in 5 years instead of 7 on

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:07.250
the Air, but when that happens, if you do
wait that long to upgrade your iPad, you won’t

00:05:07.250 --> 00:05:10.970
really mind since you enjoyed the ProMotion
tech and better speakers for all of those

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:11.970
years.

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:14.130
If you enjoyed this comparison, hit that subscribe
button!

00:05:14.130 --> 00:05:19.500
Thank for watching, and we’ll see you in
the next one!

